[{"id":101261,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/.22infinity-local.20systems.22/near/101261\">#1</a> I have a quick lazy question, maybe somebody can point me to the right place in the literature: </p>\n<p>The notion of “<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-local systems” as considered in Abad &amp; Schaetz <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4693\">arXiv:1011.4693</a> and Block &amp; Smith <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/0908.2843\">arXiv:0908.2843</a> are (when over a field of char=0)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>probably equivalent to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-functors from the fundamental <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-groupoid of the domain to the evident <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-category of chain complexes</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and probably reflect the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>-rational homotopy type of their domain</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>?</p>\n<p>Is this or something like this known/made explicit in the literature anywhere?</p>","timestamp":1663493941,"subject":"\"infinity-local systems\"","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":101296,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/.22infinity-local.20systems.22/near/101296\">#2</a> Of relevance to this is Lurie, J.. Algebraic K-theory and Manifold Topology, notes for course Math 281 in Autumn 2014. (Lectures 21 and 22), but more importantly Rivera and Zeinalian, https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.01264 in their section 5. Other relevant papers are to be found at <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Manuel%20Rivera\">Manuel Rivera</a>.</p>\n<p>Lurie’s dg-nerve of a dg-category was generalised by <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Giovanni%20Faonte\">Giovanni Faonte</a> in Simplicial nerve of an A∞-category. Theory Appl. Categ 32 (2), (2017) 31 – 52.</p>","timestamp":1663571735,"subject":"\"infinity-local systems\"","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":101321,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/.22infinity-local.20systems.22/near/101321\">#3</a> Thanks! This article by Rivera &amp; Zeinalian is insightful. I am collecting references at <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/flat%20infinity-connection\">flat infinity-connection</a></em>.</p>","timestamp":1663656802,"subject":"\"infinity-local systems\"","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":101322,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/.22infinity-local.20systems.22/near/101322\">#4</a> I alerted Manuel and Mahmoud to your question so hopefully they will contribute some things to the Lab entries.  Jim Stasheff and myself have been writing a sort of brief survey on the link between some of these ideas.  It should be on the ArXiv soon.</p>","timestamp":1663657674,"subject":"\"infinity-local systems\"","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]